            <p>Techniques for Securing a Peripheral Intravenous Catheter During Insertion.&#x000a0;The left panel demonstrates holding the hub of the intravenous catheter between the thumb and index finger. The right panel shows an alternative grip, with the index finger curled around the side port and counterpressure applied to the cap of the flashback chamber. Each method provides stability and control for successful vascular access. Contributed by Gabriel Beecham, MB BCh BAO</p>
